.TH SPORTS_NEAR_ME.YAML 5 "2026-09-13" "sports_near_me 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
sports_near_me.yaml \- config file for sports-game(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.sports_near_me.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
A YAML file of shared defaults and a per-sport
.B follow
list, read by
.BR sports-game (1)
on every invocation. Every key is optional. A command-line flag always
overrides the matching shared key; the follow list is only consulted
when no team is given on the command line.
.PP
The file is looked up at
.I ~/.sports_near_me.yaml
by default, or at the path given with
.BR sports-game 's
.B \-\-config
flag. Passing
.B \-\-config
with a path that does not exist is an error; the default path silently
not existing is not \(em most people will not have created it yet.
.SH SHARED KEYS
.TP
.B tz
IANA timezone string (e.g.
.IR America/New_York )
used for every printed kickoff time. Overridden by
.BR sports-game 's
.B \-\-tz
flag. Default:
.BR UTC \(em
never guessed from the machine's own clock, since this file can be
copied to a different machine/location. Set this to see local kickoff
times.
.TP
.B log_level
One of \fBDEBUG\fR, \fBINFO\fR, \fBWARNING\fR, \fBERROR\fR,
\fBCRITICAL\fR. Default: \fBINFO\fR.
.TP
.B log_dir
Directory to also write a timestamped diagnostic log file to. Default:
none (diagnostics go to stderr only).
.SH THE FOLLOW LIST
.B follow
is a mapping from sport key (see
.BR sports-game (1)'s
.B SPORTS
section \(em \fBnfl\fR, \fBmlb\fR, \fBnhl\fR, \fBncaaf\fR, \fBncaamb\fR,
\fBncaawb\fR, \fBncaabsb\fR, \fBncaamh\fR, \fBncaavbw\fR, \fBncaavbm\fR)
to an object with either or both of:
.TP
.B teams
A list of team names, in the same loose form
.BR sports-game (1)
accepts on the command line (nickname, city, full name, or
abbreviation).
.TP
.B conferences
A list of conference names (e.g. \fBSEC\fR, \fBBig Ten\fR, \fBACC\fR).
.B NCAA sports only
\(em \fBnfl\fR, \fBmlb\fR, and \fBnhl\fR have no conference concept
here and any entry under their
.B conferences
key is skipped with a warning, not an error.
.PP
Following a conference follows every current member team's entire
schedule, including non-conference and cross-conference games \(em not
just games against other conference members. Membership is looked up
fresh each run (see
.BR NOTES ),
so realignment is reflected automatically.
.PP
A team reachable both directly (under
.BR teams )
and via a followed conference is only shown once.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
.RS
tz: America/New_York
log_level: INFO
# log_dir: ~/.sports_near_me/logs

follow:
  nfl:
    teams: [Bears]
  mlb:
    teams: [Cubs]
  nhl:
    teams: [Blackhawks]
  ncaaf:
    teams: [Notre Dame]          # independent \- not in any conference
    conferences: [SEC, Big Ten]
  ncaamb:
    conferences: [ACC]            # every ACC team \- Duke, UNC, Louisville...
  ncaawb:
    teams: [Duke]
.RE
.fi
.SH NOTES
Nothing under
.B follow
is, or ever becomes, a stored id. Every team and conference name here is
re-resolved against ESPN's live data on each run of
.BR sports-game (1);
this file only ever holds what a person typed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sports-game (1)
